heroic:
A blind worm here dug tunnels to the light,
And there a seed, racked with heroic pain,
Thrust eager tentacles to sun and rain;

hero:
Here in my heart I am Helen;
I'm Aspasia and Hero, at least.
I'm Judith, and Jael, and Madame de Staël;

herrings:
Peaches grow wild, and pigs can live in clover;
A barrel of salted herrings lasts a year;
The spring begins before the winter's over.

herb:
If such as I, might grow upon the hills;
And whether such poor herb sufficed to grow,
For Romney Leigh to break his fast upon ’t,—

hereafter:
With problems that still remain;
But think in the great hereafter
Their meaning will all be plain.

herein:
That you requite me not is plain to see;
Myself your slave herein have I confessed:
Thus far, indeed, the world may mock at me;

heralded:
Some are swaddled in silk and down,
And heralded by a star;
They swathed my limbs in a sackcloth gown

heralds:
What if my heart be in the blast
That heralds his triumphant way;
Shall I repine, shall I not say:

hern:
A widower he was, an' Sal was thinkin' 'at she 'd wing him;
I reckon he was wond'rin' what them rings o' hern would bring him.
An' when the spellin'-test commenced, he up an' took his station,

hermonax:
gift of sea wrack;
I, Hermonax, offer it
to thee, Ino,
